* Stage A snapshot 20261110-084324-e8a2a7b (issue #295): everything needed to reproduce the bench

*==== consumer_load.inc ====
* consumer_load.inc -- the gf180-buck error-amplifier load of record, for the
* Stage A probe of spec/decision-records/0008 (issue #295).
*
* SOURCE (read-only, copied verbatim, ideal parts, "nothing here is measured"):
*   2AMLogic/gf180-buck  design/netlists/compensator.spice  (type-III, Venable)
*   read 2026-11-10 at gf180-buck main b671d9e38321873caa9574f553d05473844c8bfc;
*   identical to the network quoted in DR-0008 section 2.1 (read 2026-11-06).
*   Original nodes: VOUT=vbuck, FBN=fbn, VC=vc, GND=0.
*
*   Rtop VOUT FBN 10k ; R3 VOUT X 204 ; C3 X FBN 780p ; Rbot FBN GND 5k
*   R2 FBN Z 4.55k ; C1 Z VC 1.75n ; C2 FBN VC 35.7p
*   XEA VDD33 GND VREF FBN VC IBIAS opamp_two_stage   (the DUT, instantiated
*   by each bench as Xdut, never here)
*
* A changed consumer netlist reopens DR-0008 section 2.1; it is not silently
* followed. Re-read the source before re-running (record states the sha).

.subckt ea_load vbuck fbn vc
Rtop vbuck fbn 10k
R3 vbuck x 204
C3 x fbn 780p
Rbot fbn 0 5k
R2 fbn z 4.55k
C1 z vc 1.75n
C2 fbn vc 35.7p
.ends ea_load

* PWM-comparator input on VC (DR-0008 item C3, consumer has not confirmed a
* value). The consumer's pwm_comp.spice XCPM1 (nfet_03v3 L=1u W=8u, gate = VC)
* is the only thing VC drives there. Its drain/source/bulk are tied to ground
* here, so this is the gate-channel + overlap capacitance of the device at the
* VC bias, an APPROXIMATION of the comparator input (in the real circuit D is a
* diode-connected PMOS node and S the tail node). Status: assumed.
.subckt pwm_in vc
XCPM1 0 vc 0 0 nfet_03v3 L=1u W=8u nf=1 ad='int((nf+1)/2) * W/nf * 0.18u' as='int((nf+2)/2) * W/nf * 0.18u' pd='2*int((nf+1)/2) * (W/nf + 0.18u)' ps='2*int((nf+2)/2) * (W/nf + 0.18u)' nrd='0.18u / W' nrs='0.18u / W' sa=0 sb=0 sd=0 m=1
.ends pwm_in

*==== tb_region.spice ====
* tb_region.spice -- Stage A step 1: CLOSURE-INDEPENDENT region check
* (spec/decision-records/0008, section 4 "DC operating-point method" item 1).
*
* No loop to close: VC is forced by an ideal source at the bias level, FBN
* (the amplifier's inverting input) and VREF (non-inverting) both at 0.6 V, the
* common mode the consumer applies. `.op` then reports the regions and
* currents of XM1/XM2/XM5 (input pair and tail do not depend on VC). The
* consumer network is not instantiated: FBN and VC are forced, so it would be
* inert at DC. The DUT is the committed export via `opamp_two_stage.dut.spice`.

.include 'design.ngspice'
.include 'opamp_two_stage.dut.spice'

.param vcb=1.40 vref=0.6

Vdd vdd 0 dc 3.3
Ibias vdd ibias dc 10u
Vref vinp 0 dc {vref}
Vfbn fbn 0 dc {vref}
Vvc vc 0 dc {vcb}
Xdut vdd 0 vinp fbn vc ibias opamp_two_stage

*==== tb_ac.spice ====
* tb_ac.spice -- Stage A step 2: small-signal bench, DC-closed / AC-open
* (spec/decision-records/0008, section 4 "DC operating-point method" item 2).
*
* The amplifier drives the REAL consumer load (consumer_load.inc) plus the
* PWM-comparator input. A huge inductor Lfb in series with a DC source Vset =
* VC_bias - VREF from VC to FBN servos the amplifier to the bias point at DC
* (FBN = VREF, VC = VC_bias) and is open at every swept frequency (technique
* of sim/gain-gbw-pm/README.md "Measurement technique"). The buck output node
* is an ideal 1.8 V source (AC ground). The 1 V AC stimulus sits on vinp.
* Aol(f) = v(vc) / (v(vinp) - v(fbn)), the ACTUAL differential phasor.
*
* The `.param` line is rewritten by the driver ONLY for the isolation study
* (lfb) and the VC_bias +-0.15 V runs (vcb).
* The DUT is the committed export; no transistor is declared here.

.include 'design.ngspice'
.include 'opamp_two_stage.dut.spice'
.include 'consumer_load.inc'

.param lfb=1e9 vcb=1.40 vref=0.6 vbuck=1.8

Vdd vdd 0 dc 3.3
Ibias vdd ibias dc 10u
Vref vinp 0 dc {vref} ac 1
Vbuck vbuck 0 dc {vbuck}
Xdut vdd 0 vinp fbn vc ibias opamp_two_stage
Xload vbuck fbn vc ea_load
Xpwm vc pwm_in
Lfb vc nset {lfb}
Vset nset fbn dc {vcb - vref}

*==== tb_beta.spice ====
* tb_beta.spice -- Stage A step 2b: 1/beta(f) from the passive network ALONE
* (spec/decision-records/0008, section 4). The amplifier is removed; an ideal
* AC source drives VC, the buck output node is AC ground, and beta = v(fbn) /
* v(vc), so 1/beta = v(vc) / v(fbn). The amplifier's own input capacitance on
* FBN is not in this bench (it is inside Aol's measurement); the difference is
* femtofarad-class against the 35.7 pF of C2 and is stated in the record.

.include 'design.ngspice'
.include 'consumer_load.inc'

Vbuck vbuck 0 dc 0
Vtest vc 0 dc 0 ac 1
Xload vbuck fbn vc ea_load

